# Normalise line endings.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF on Windows breaks inside a Linux
# container in a way that reads as a missing interpreter: `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`
# makes the kernel look for an executable literally named "bash\r", and the
# container logs `env: can't execute 'bash': No such file or directory`. That
# cost a debugging cycle during the Docker bring-up, and it is entirely
# preventable.
*               text=auto

# Anything a Linux kernel or shell interprets must be LF, regardless of platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env*           text eol=lf
*.prisma        text eol=lf

# Windows-only tooling stays CRLF.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary

# Generated by scripts/ci/cdc-harness.mjs, which writes LF and then compares the
# committed file byte-for-byte. With `text=auto` git hands Windows a CRLF copy,
# the comparison fails, and the gate reports drift that no re-recording can fix
# — the same fight prettier was having with these files.
**/cdc/expectations.json -text
